  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.22,
      "text": " The CIA drugged its own citizens, and they admitted it."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.72,
      "end": 11.34,
      "text": " Starting in 1953, a secret program called MKUltra tested LSD and other drugs on people."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.92,
      "end": 13.58,
      "text": " Some of them never knew they'd been dosed."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.12,
      "end": 18.12,
      "text": " The goal? Mind control, and making people talk under interrogation."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.16,
      "end": 23.02,
      "text": " In 1973, the CIA director ordered the files destroyed,"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.52,
      "end": 28.6,
      "text": " but about twenty thousand documents survived because they had been misfiled with financial records."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.6,
      "end": 30.98,
      "text": " They were found in 1977."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.86,
      "end": 33.94,
      "text": " So, what else do you think got shredded?"
    }
  ],
